    },
    {
      "name": "sugar substitute (stevia)",
      "amount": "1/8 tsp",
      "notes": "optional"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Dice the onion and mince the garlic and grate the ginger.",
    "Heat a pot over medium heat and add a splash of oil, then sauté the onion, garlic, ginger, and ground annatto for 3 minutes until fragrant.",
    "Pour in the fish stock, water, sea salt, pepper, and sugar substitute, and bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Add the cod fillets and let the broth simmer for 6 minutes until the fish is cooked through.",
    "Stir in fresh dill and lemon juice, then reduce heat to low and allow the broth to rest for 2 minutes.",
    "Strain the broth through a fine sieve to remove solids, creating a clear glassy consistency.",
    "Serve the broth warm, garnished with a sprinkle of dill, and enjoy the floral aroma."
